From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mali_kbase: port hrtimer_init_on_stack()+.function to hrtimer_setup_on_stack()

Same removal as patch 0006 (hrtimer_init()+timer->function assignment
replaced by a single hrtimer_setup() call on kernel 7.2), but for the
on-stack variant: hrtimer_init_on_stack(timer, clock_id, mode) is gone,
replaced by hrtimer_setup_on_stack(timer, function, clock_id, mode)
(confirmed in include/linux/hrtimer.h on this kernel). Patch 0006's
call-site inventory missed this one because it only matched
`hrtimer_init(`, not the on-stack variant, and this call site
(kbase_pm_do_reset's reset-timeout watchdog) was unreached at compile
time until patch 0008 fixed the CONFIG_MALI_DEVFREQ propagation bug
that was blocking the build before it got this far.

Only one call site in the whole driver (confirmed by grep for
hrtimer_init_on_stack across the full tree). Same faithful 1:1
semantic replacement as 0006: the ->function assignment happened
immediately after hrtimer_init_on_stack() and before hrtimer_start(),
so folding it into hrtimer_setup_on_stack()'s function argument changes
nothing about ordering or behavior.

Fixes the mali_kbase.ko build against kernel 7.2.0-rc4-sky1-ncz (next
error after 0008 unblocked the devfreq translation units).

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c
@@ -4285,8 +4285,8 @@
 	rtdata.timed_out = false;
 
 	/* Create a timer to use as a timeout on the reset */
-	hrtimer_init_on_stack(&rtdata.timer, CLOCK_MONOTONIC, HRTIMER_MODE_REL);
-	rtdata.timer.function = kbasep_reset_timeout;
+	hrtimer_setup_on_stack(&rtdata.timer, kbasep_reset_timeout, CLOCK_MONOTONIC,
+				HRTIMER_MODE_REL);
 
 	hrtimer_start(&rtdata.timer, HR_TIMER_DELAY_MSEC(RESET_TIMEOUT), HRTIMER_MODE_REL);
 
